2223|n|A very small twist of flax, wool, cotton, silk, or other fibrous substance, drawn out to considerable length; a compound cord consisting of two or more single yarns doubled, or joined together, and twisted. ; A filament, as of a flower, or of any fibrous substance, as of bark; also, a line of gold or silver. ; The prominent part of the spiral of a screw or nut; the rib. See Screw, n., 1. ; Fig.: Something continued in a long course or tenor; a,s the thread of life, or of a discourse. ; Fig.: Composition; quality; fineness.	a:23de,78,2;1x89,55,4;1ru6,25,6~1ru6,25,6;1x89,55,4;23de,78,2	V:28ua,6,6~28ua,6,6	n:rc,100,6;23de,78,2;1hhn,39,5;1xig,37,5;1st7,34,3~rc,100,6;1hhn,39,5;1xig,37,5;1st7,34,3;23de,78,2	N:16ms,102,3;uba,67,5;1j5t,64,4;20qx,43,5;1v0x,30,3~20qx,43,5;uba,67,5;1j5t,64,4;1v0x,30,3;16ms,102,3
2223|a|A very small twist of flax, wool, cotton, silk, or other fibrous substance, drawn out to considerable length; a compound cord consisting of two or more single yarns doubled, or joined together, and twisted. ; A filament, as of a flower, or of any fibrous substance, as of bark; also, a line of gold or silver. ; The prominent part of the spiral of a screw or nut; the rib. See Screw, n., 1. ; Fig.: Something continued in a long course or tenor; a,s the thread of life, or of a discourse. ; Fig.: Composition; quality; fineness.	j:1j5t,44,1~1j5t,44,1
