2235|n|The plank, stone, or piece of timber, which lies under a door, especially of a dwelling house, church, temple, or the like; the doorsill; hence, entrance; gate; door. ; Fig.: The place or point of entering or beginning, entrance; outset; as, the threshold of life.	a:bn5,79,6~bn5,79,6
